From 52c65a2cc0bad8d31b061cb2df199a94acb8e502 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Huiwen He <hehuiwen@kylinos.cn>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:32:23 +0800
Subject: [RFC PATCH v2 8/8] ksmbd: experiment with RX-owned WRITE response
 sending

WRITE workers can contend with the receiver on the same TCP socket.
Let the receiver send completed WRITE responses, controlled by the
default-off write_tx_rx_owner parameter.

Send one frame at a time from its existing iov. Use nonblocking sends
in RX and retain the work and iterator for TX-worker continuation.
Track ownership with a locked IDLE/DRAINING/DEFERRED state and keep one
owner reference until draining finishes. Notify RX when ownership starts
or returns from the continuation.

Drain before TCP receives and while waiting for request slots. Preserve
frame serialization, the response budget and receive-attempt deadlines.
Worker-owned response coalescing remains unchanged.

Built with W=1. Extracted-function ASan/UBSan and kernel transport checks
passed, including FIN, paused readers, mixed replies, reset, shutdown
and short-send recovery. Short fio comparisons preserved 1 MiB WRITE
throughput. One 4 KiB slowdown did not repeat in three further pairs;
its cause remains unresolved.

Signed-off-by: Huiwen He <hehuiwen@kylinos.cn>
